data/texts/ holds excerpts of public-domain works, from Project Gutenberg: Jane Austen, Pride and
Prejudice (eBook 1342); Arthur Conan Doyle, The Adventures of Sherlock Holmes (eBook 1661); and
H. G. Wells, The Time Machine (eBook 35). Each file's header, or for Wells its source record,
names the edition used.

The digits of the challenge in data/cells.json are those of the 1939 first edition of Alexander
d'Agapeyeff's Codes and Ciphers, as transcribed on the English Wikipedia page for the cipher.
